message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ResistaMet GUI: An Open-Source Electrical Measurement Suite for Keithley 2400-family Sourcemeters"
abstract: >
  ResistaMet GUI is an open-source desktop application for electrical
  characterization with Keithley 2400-family sourcemeters (2400, 2401, 2410,
  2420, 2425, 2430, 2440, and 2450). It provides six measurement modes on a
  single instrument: continuous 2- or 4-wire resistance, DC voltage source,
  DC current source, multi-spot four-point probe with ASTM F84-aligned
  geometry corrections (with optional current-reversal/delta mode),
  hardware-driven I-V sweep, and van der Pauw via the ASTM F76 eight-reading
  protocol with an f(Q) homogeneity check. Per-reading instrument uncertainty
  from the Keithley datasheet propagates through every derived quantity
  (sheet resistance, resistivity, conductivity). Measurement output is
  streamed to a self-describing data file with full provenance metadata.
